# column#0 and row#0 are each the scene's ONLY container of their kind,
# which makes ordinal naming safe across languages. THE SHARE ARITHMETIC
# (docs/traps.md points back at it): a share under a platform's minimum
# control size measures the minimum, not the contract — the textarea's
# 96pt floor binds, GTK's 34pt button height next, and the 540x330
# window's 16pt inset leaves tracks of ~63/126/63 at 25/50/25.
expect label#0 "grow probe"
# NOT REDUNDANT (DESIGN.md holds the rules): shares are percentages of
# the children's SUM, so a hugging root divides nothing and every share
# still passes.
expect_root_fills
# A container can pool leftover as slack BESIDE its children with the
# ratios intact. This also gates the row's 12-unit gap, since children
# PLUS GAPS must span the box, and shares cannot see spacing at all.
expect_fills column#0
expect_fills row#0
# Three backends read a share off the TRACK, so a widget with a
# HARD-CODED size (240x96 frozen in the SwiftUI frame and WinUI's
# Height) splits its container exactly right and renders wrong.
expect_fills textarea#0
# The grown LEAVES: a grower renders AT its track (DESIGN.md, ruled
# 2026-08-22), and SwiftUI — the one proposal-negotiating backend — must
# be told per kind.
expect_fills label#1
expect_fills button#0
expect_shares column#0 "25,50,25"
expect_shares row#0 "25,75"
